      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لوّث التِّبْنَ بِالقَتِّ</span></b>  <i>He mixed the straw with</i>
[<i>the kind of trefoil called</i>] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قتّ</span>. (A.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لوّث</span>
<i>He,</i> or <i>it, rendered</i> water <i>turbid.</i> (S.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لوّث</span>,
inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَلْوِيثٌ</span>, <i>He befouled, defiled, polluted,
dirtied, soiled, besmeared,</i> or <i>bedaubed,</i> (S, K,)
his clothes with mud. (S.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  See 1 and 8.

